---
import Legal from '../layouts/Legal.astro';
import { site } from '../content/site';
const co = site.legalName;
---
<Legal title="Privacy Policy" updated="October 4, 2026" description={`How ${site.name} collects, uses and protects your information.`}>
  <p>This policy explains what information {co} ("Clear Veil", "we", "us") collects through clearveilmarketing.com (the "Site"), how we use it, and the choices you have.</p>

  <h2>1. Information we collect</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Information you give us:</strong> When you use our contact form, we collect your name, email address, business or website, monthly ad budget range, and your message. If you book a call, our scheduling provider collects the details you enter there.</li>
    <li><strong>Device and usage data:</strong> We and our analytics providers may automatically collect information such as your IP address, device type, operating system, browser type, pages visited and how you arrived at the Site.</li>
    <li><strong>Cookies and similar technologies:</strong> We may use cookies, pixels and similar tools, including Google Tag Manager, Google Analytics and the Meta Pixel, to understand Site traffic and measure the performance of our advertising. You can manage or block cookies through your browser settings.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>2. How we use your information</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Responding to you:</strong> To reply to your enquiry, schedule calls and provide the services you ask about.</li>
    <li><strong>Improving the Site:</strong> To understand how visitors use the Site and make it better.</li>
    <li><strong>Advertising measurement:</strong> To measure whether our own ads lead to enquiries, and to show relevant ads on platforms such as Meta and Google.</li>
    <li><strong>Security:</strong> To protect the Site from spam, abuse and fraud.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>3. Sharing and disclosure</h2>
  <p>We do not sell or rent your personal information. We share it only in these cases:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Service providers:</strong> Companies that help us run the Site and our business, such as website hosting (Vercel), email delivery (Resend), scheduling (Cal.com), and analytics and advertising (Google and Meta). They may only use your information to provide services to us.</li>
    <li><strong>Legal requirements:</strong> If required by law or in response to valid legal requests.</li>
    <li><strong>Business transfers:</strong> If our business is involved in a merger, acquisition or sale of assets, your information may be transferred as part of that transaction.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>4. Data security</h2>
  <p>We take reasonable measures to protect your information from unauthorized access, disclosure or alteration. No online service is completely secure, so we cannot guarantee absolute security.</p>

  <h2>5. Your rights and choices</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Access:</strong> You can ask what information we hold about you.</li>
    <li><strong>Correction:</strong> You can ask us to correct inaccurate information.</li>
    <li><strong>Deletion:</strong> You can ask us to delete your information, subject to legal obligations.</li>
    <li><strong>Opt-out:</strong> You can opt out of personalized advertising through your Meta and Google ad settings, and block cookies in your browser.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>6. Third-party links</h2>
  <p>The Site links to third-party websites and services. We are not responsible for their privacy practices, so please review their policies.</p>

  <h2>7. Children's privacy</h2>
  <p>The Site is not intended for anyone under 13. We do not knowingly collect personal information from children. If we learn we have, we will delete it.</p>

  <h2>8. Changes to this policy</h2>
  <p>We may update this policy from time to time. Changes will be posted on this page with a new "last updated" date.</p>

  <h2>9. Contact us</h2>
  <p>Questions about this policy or your information? Reach us through the <a href="/#contact">contact form</a>.</p>
</Legal>
